# ==============================================================================
# Project docs (private planning material — not part of the shipped repo)
# ==============================================================================
## docs/* (not docs/) ignores direct children while still letting git
## traverse the directory to evaluate the negations below. A bare `docs/`
## rule excludes the directory itself, which git will not descend into even
## to check per-file negations — the classic gitignore gotcha.
docs/*
## Portfolio artifacts a reviewer should be able to find, tracked despite
## the blanket rule above. Everything else in docs/ (planning notes,
## the implementation plan) stays private.
!docs/SECURITY.md
!docs/DECISIONS.md

# ==============================================================================
# macOS
# ==============================================================================
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ==============================================================================
# Xcode / iOS / Swift
# ==============================================================================

## User-specific Xcode state (never shared between machines)
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xccheckout

## Legacy Xcode per-user files (pre-workspace era, harmless to keep excluded)
*.pbxuser
*.mode1v3
*.mode2v3
*.perspectivev3
!default.pbxuser
!default.mode1v3
!default.mode2v3
!default.perspectivev3

## Build products & derived data
build/
DerivedData/
*.moved-aside
*.hmap
*.ipa
*.dSYM
*.dSYM.zip

## Swift Package Manager
## .build/ and .swiftpm/ are local resolution/build state, always regenerable.
## Package.resolved is INTENTIONALLY NOT ignored — for an app target (not a
## library) it should be committed so every clone builds against identical
## dependency versions.
.build/
.swiftpm/
Packages/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/

## Xcode Previews / Simulator scratch state
*.xcresult/
Preview Content/PreviewAssets.xcassets/.DS_Store

## Instruments / Profiling
*.trace

## Playgrounds
timeline.xctimeline
playground.xcworkspace

## App Store Connect / signing artifacts — never commit these
*.mobileprovision
*.p12
*.p8
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest

## fastlane (only relevant if it gets added later; harmless if unused)
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots/**/*.png
fastlane/test_output

